{"name":"Black Drop","hex":"#90abd9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black drop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A narcotic preparation consisting essentially of a solution of opium in vinegar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_drop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black drop effect","blocks":[{"text":"The black drop effect is an optical phenomenon visible during a transit of Venus and, to a lesser extent, a transit of Mercury."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Venustransit_2004-06-08_07-44.jpg/330px-Venustransit_2004-06-08_07-44.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_drop_effect","wikidata":"Q1367380"},{"title":"Laudanum","blocks":[{"text":"Laudanum is a tincture of opium containing approximately 10% powdered opium by weight. Laudanum is prepared by dissolving extracts from the opium poppy in alcohol (ethanol)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Laudanum.jpeg/330px-Laudanum.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laudanum","wikidata":"Q898739"},{"title":"Drop (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Drop is a 2025 American mystery thriller film directed by Christopher Landon and written by Jillian Jacobs and Chris Roach. It stars Meghann Fahy, Brandon Sklenar, Violett Beane, and Jeffery Self. In the film, a widowed mother receives threatening messages during her first date in years, which causes her to question her date and fear for her safety."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Drop_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drop_(film)","wikidata":"Q125983478"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png/120px-Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png/250px-Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png/120px-Venus_Black_Drop_effect.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVenus_Black_Drop_effect.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Venus_Drawing.jpg/120px-Venus_Drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Venus_Drawing.jpg/250px-Venus_Drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Venus_Drawing.jpg/120px-Venus_Drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVenus_Drawing.jpg"},{"s